# Prettier exclusions.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GENERATED ARTIFACTS UNDER A BYTE-COMPARISON DRIFT GATE
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Some artifacts are emitted by a generator and then byte-compared against a
# fresh regeneration by a release gate. Generators do not emit prettier-styled
# output, so formatting such a file makes the gate fail on the NEXT
# regeneration — the artifact on disk no longer equals what the generator
# produces, and the diff is pure whitespace.
#
# The failure is worse than it sounds because it is misattributed: a formatter
# pass over an unrelated change turns the generator tests and the release
# preflight red, and every one of those failures points at the change under
# test rather than at the formatter that actually caused them.
#
# THE RULE: if you add a generated artifact with a drift gate, add it here in
# the same commit as the generator. Not afterwards, and not when the gate first
# goes red.
#
# This repository currently has no such artifacts. The section stays, with this
# note, so the first one has an obvious home and its author has the reason.

